					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/falling-objects" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1743723); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1743723&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349844" alt="Falling Objects" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1743723)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/falling-objects" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1743723); return false;" >Falling Objects</a></span> <span class="odate time_1382894791 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Oct 2013 17:26</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1879329">
									

<p>I feel as if one of the major contributors to this issue is the &quot;Nothing is canon, everything is canon&quot; policy.</p>
<p>Want to introduce a pope like figure to the church of the broken god? Unless you pull out an absolutely amazing piece of writing, everybody decries it as you trying to enforce your ideas on the canon.</p>
<p>To pull up an actual example, SCP-1716. A great SCP on it's own, well written, and fits perfectly into what MC&amp;D would offer to its clientele. I upvoted because it was a great article. But some people openly stated in the discussion section of the thread that they downvoted simply because a face was put to Mr. Dark.</p>

							</div>

								
