														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1879472">
									

<p>Personally, I don't see most Chaos Insurgency employees as bad people, on a personal scale. The CI as I see them does require certain individuals who aren't afraid to get their hands ethically dirty, but that's a consequence of their reduced resources &#8212; the Foundation would do the same things to survive in the areas that the CI call home. And if they had to choose between &quot;no exploiting anomalies&quot; and &quot;containment fails on a large scale&quot;, like the CI, which lacks the connections and resources of the Foundation, might have to, they'd sacrifice the first tenet long before the second.</p>
<p>Really, the only thing keeping the CI from being an interesting and complex organization is the Saturday-morning-cartoon name.</p>

